cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this detection content, please cite it as below."
title: "Borrowed Trust: Detection Content for Three Concurrent Signed-Binary Sideload Campaigns"
abstract: >-
  Deployable detection content for three concurrent August 2026 campaigns that share a single
  execution primitive: a validly signed or otherwise trusted binary resolves a malicious
  dependency at runtime. Covers the BoryptGrab-lineage infostealer distributed through
  approximately 292 brand-impersonation GitHub repositories, the QuickFox VPN supply chain
  compromise delivering the FDMTP implant, and the "Free VPN for PC" GitHub repository
  delivering Lumma Stealer. Includes Sigma, YARA, KQL, Splunk SPL, and Suricata rules, two
  read-only PowerShell hunt scripts, a consolidated indicator set, and an explicit ledger of
  what this class of campaign makes structurally undetectable. Defensive material only.
type: software
